1
00:00:00,106 --> 00:00:01,106
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

2
00:00:01,106 --> 00:00:02,106
[Child and animal scenes filmed safely]

3
00:00:02,106 --> 00:00:02,971
[under the guardian
and expert supervision per guidelines]

4
00:00:03,139 --> 00:00:05,375
[Episode 4]

5
00:00:12,491 --> 00:00:14,116
[Durumi Electronics Sales Team Workshop]

6
00:00:17,987 --> 00:00:21,138
- Hey, Manager Lee. Get me a latte.
- Okay.

7
00:00:26,584 --> 00:00:28,438
Mr. Han!

8
00:00:28,438 --> 00:00:31,594
Hey, not sure if you remember.

9
00:00:31,594 --> 00:00:33,610
But we made a bet yesterday while drinking.

10
00:00:33,610 --> 00:00:37,322
The first one to pass out
had to buy snacks at the rest area.

11
00:00:37,322 --> 00:00:39,054
Mr. Bong.

12
00:00:39,054 --> 00:00:40,754
Team Leader Bong.

13
00:00:41,642 --> 00:00:43,711
Here you go.

14
00:00:43,711 --> 00:00:46,202
Oh, thank you, Mr. Han.

15
00:00:46,202 --> 00:00:48,694
I'll go easy on your card.

16
00:00:48,694 --> 00:00:51,254
No, just go all out.

17
00:00:51,254 --> 00:00:52,511
Just go big. Go big.

18
00:00:52,511 --> 00:00:55,911
All right, I'll go big.

19
00:00:57,030 --> 00:01:00,278
Everyone, let's go eat!

20
00:01:00,914 --> 00:01:02,782
What's with me?

21
00:01:02,782 --> 00:01:06,078
Why am I scared of him?

22
00:01:30,814 --> 00:01:34,478
What? Did I dream something last night?

23
00:01:36,311 --> 00:01:38,434
Oh, my, I have heartburn.

24
00:01:38,434 --> 00:01:41,845
Oh, why does my shoulder hurt so much?

25
00:01:42,626 --> 00:01:44,578
Oh, dear, my neck.

26
00:01:45,470 --> 00:01:47,046
- Director Yoo!
- What?

27
00:01:47,046 --> 00:01:49,618
Have some of this first.

28
00:01:49,618 --> 00:01:51,358
A hangover cure?

29
00:01:51,358 --> 00:01:54,426
I don't get hangovers. You have it.

30
00:01:54,426 --> 00:01:57,745
Oh, you don't have one.

31
00:01:58,426 --> 00:02:01,422
You were amazing yesterday, Director.

32
00:02:01,422 --> 00:02:03,902
Why? Did something happen yesterday?

33
00:02:03,902 --> 00:02:07,178
No, nothing.

34
00:02:10,145 --> 00:02:12,978
Oh, good work.

35
00:02:13,734 --> 00:02:16,911
It was your first scene,
so you were a bit flustered, right?

36
00:02:17,974 --> 00:02:19,674
You did well.

37
00:02:20,486 --> 00:02:22,378
Thank you.

38
00:02:24,346 --> 00:02:27,354
Director, can I ask you something?

39
00:02:27,354 --> 00:02:28,354
What is it?

40
00:02:28,354 --> 00:02:30,346
Why'd we handle those guys
like that yesterday?

41
00:02:30,346 --> 00:02:32,562
It was different from other meetings.

42
00:02:32,562 --> 00:02:36,045
Didn't you hear? It was a pre-meeting.

43
00:02:53,529 --> 00:02:55,278
Oh, my back...

44
00:03:05,974 --> 00:03:07,014
They turned themselves in?

45
00:03:07,014 --> 00:03:10,145
We got a call at the station
as soon as the sun came up.

46
00:03:10,145 --> 00:03:12,278
The old man said he wanted to surrender.

47
00:03:12,278 --> 00:03:14,878
And he confessed to everything
without even being asked.

48
00:03:14,878 --> 00:03:16,594
He admitted they harvested the organs

49
00:03:16,594 --> 00:03:18,245
from all seven missing victims
and buried them.

50
00:03:18,245 --> 00:03:19,866
He even gave them the burial sites.

51
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:21,754
He said it all happened in that warehouse.

52
00:03:21,754 --> 00:03:24,345
The crime scene investigator
is currently collecting DNA samples.

53
00:03:24,345 --> 00:03:27,382
But why are they all in such bad shape?

54
00:03:27,382 --> 00:03:31,011
Apparently they got into a fight
and beat each other up.

55
00:03:31,011 --> 00:03:32,538
Bad enough to end up like this?

56
00:03:32,538 --> 00:03:33,882
Well, we can't know the reason

57
00:03:33,882 --> 00:03:35,545
because no one will say
what they fought over.

58
00:03:35,545 --> 00:03:37,578
Anyway, that's what they said happened.

59
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:58,918
What about recent guests?

60
00:03:58,918 --> 00:04:00,894
They hadn't been operating
for the past month,

61
00:04:00,894 --> 00:04:02,130
so there were no guests.

62
00:04:02,130 --> 00:04:03,438
So there wasn't a guest list either.

63
00:04:03,438 --> 00:04:05,426
Did you check the CCTV?

64
00:04:05,426 --> 00:04:07,650
Oh, well...

65
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:11,278
That's the strange part. Nothing's there.

66
00:04:11,278 --> 00:04:13,706
What do you mean? Was it erased?

67
00:04:13,706 --> 00:04:15,611
Well, they said they turned it off.

68
00:04:15,611 --> 00:04:19,290
We don't know whether
it was deleted or never existed.

69
00:04:19,290 --> 00:04:22,550
In 15 years as a detective, I've never
had a case handed to me this easily.

70
00:04:22,550 --> 00:04:25,550
We've got the scene, the evidence,
and the confession.

71
00:04:25,550 --> 00:04:27,445
CCTV or not, it doesn't matter.

72
00:04:30,230 --> 00:04:32,311
No, just...

73
00:04:32,573 --> 00:04:35,743
[Inspection in Progress, Reduce Speed]

74
00:04:42,334 --> 00:04:44,538
Step out of the vehicle.

75
00:04:44,538 --> 00:04:46,874
I said, step out.

76
00:04:46,874 --> 00:04:49,242
I told you, it's urgent.
That's why we have to hurry.

77
00:04:49,242 --> 00:04:51,122
We're responding to an emergency call.

78
00:04:51,122 --> 00:04:54,942
That's why I'm asking you to show me your ID.

79
00:04:54,942 --> 00:04:57,738
Oh, you're really dedicated.
Just let us through.

80
00:04:57,738 --> 00:05:00,511
Come on, where do you think you're going?

81
00:05:00,511 --> 00:05:01,945
Someone's dying right now.

82
00:05:01,945 --> 00:05:04,945
I need to perform CPR. Have a good day.

83
00:05:04,945 --> 00:05:08,411
I understand. Just show me your ID.

84
00:05:10,644 --> 00:05:11,790
Arrest him! Get him!

85
00:05:11,790 --> 00:05:13,068
- Show me your ID! Grab him!
- Darn it.

86
00:05:15,722 --> 00:05:16,970
Yeah, Beom, what's going on?

87
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:19,706
We were checking an ambulance
heading towards the pension.

88
00:05:19,706 --> 00:05:22,911
And the man inside suddenly tried to run,
so we caught him.

89
00:05:22,911 --> 00:05:26,178
He was wearing a doctor's gown.
Looks like he's the organ-harvesting surgeon.

90
00:05:26,178 --> 00:05:28,611
- The surgeon?
- Come on. Show me your ID. Hurry up.

91
00:05:28,611 --> 00:05:30,986
Huh? Get him!

92
00:05:30,986 --> 00:05:32,730
- Hurry, show me your ID!
- Okay.

93
00:05:32,730 --> 00:05:34,430
What's his name?

94
00:05:35,118 --> 00:05:36,845
Jo Dong Min?

95
00:05:36,845 --> 00:05:39,154
It's not Jo Dong Min.

96
00:05:39,154 --> 00:05:42,578
It's Jo Dong Man. Man.

97
00:05:44,034 --> 00:05:46,190
He says it's Jo Dong Man.
Did you check his ID?

98
00:05:46,190 --> 00:05:48,722
Mr. Jo here is quite skilled.

99
00:05:48,722 --> 00:05:51,546
So clients are supposed to
come once every hour.

100
00:05:51,546 --> 00:05:56,474
Just wait at the entrance to the pension
and catch them one by one.

101
00:05:56,474 --> 00:05:58,174
Got it.

102
00:06:00,622 --> 00:06:04,211
Keep checking vehicles.
A buyer's coming every hour.

103
00:06:11,730 --> 00:06:14,690
<i>Where did all these darn flies come from?</i>

104
00:06:14,690 --> 00:06:16,390
<i>Flies?</i>

105
00:06:17,734 --> 00:06:19,778
Die, you punk!

106
00:06:37,718 --> 00:06:39,745
Get on your knees, you punk!

107
00:06:44,058 --> 00:06:46,078
<i>Get on your knees, you punk!</i>

108
00:06:52,478 --> 00:06:54,950
Hey, get on your knees.

109
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,406
Get on your knees! Hurry!

110
00:06:56,406 --> 00:06:58,545
Kneel down, you punks!

111
00:07:07,822 --> 00:07:10,826
Isn't handing them over to the police
just a waste of time?

112
00:07:10,826 --> 00:07:14,011
They won't be properly punished anyway.

113
00:07:15,386 --> 00:07:16,398
How do you know that?

114
00:07:16,398 --> 00:07:19,802
Whether they'll be punished or not.

115
00:07:19,802 --> 00:07:24,262
Do you just distrust and resent the police,
the law, and the courts by default?

116
00:07:24,262 --> 00:07:27,411
No, well, not exactly like that, but...

117
00:07:27,411 --> 00:07:30,878
A pre-meeting means
we let the law handle it first.

118
00:07:30,878 --> 00:07:34,645
It's about respecting its role
and responsibility.

119
00:07:35,442 --> 00:07:39,085
Of course, the system has its limits.

120
00:07:39,085 --> 00:07:43,654
Sometimes verdicts result in
only minimal punishment.

121
00:07:43,654 --> 00:07:47,486
And sometimes,
those who have no business interfering

122
00:07:47,486 --> 00:07:50,059
end up obstructing rightful justice.

123
00:07:50,059 --> 00:07:54,125
But that doesn't mean we should
dismiss the system entirely, right?

124
00:07:54,125 --> 00:07:57,378
We're not trying to create
a lawless world, are we?

125
00:07:59,145 --> 00:08:04,602
I think they do their job, and we do ours.

126
00:08:04,602 --> 00:08:08,845
Sometimes we simply do what they cannot.

127
00:08:11,942 --> 00:08:13,678
Director Yoo!

128
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,290
But then again, who knows.

129
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:26,878
Someday, today's pre-meeting
might become an official one.

130
00:08:28,954 --> 00:08:31,278
If they forget about us.

131
00:08:35,611 --> 00:08:41,311
<i>If they forget that there are forces
more terrifying than the law.</i>

132
00:08:46,445 --> 00:08:48,832
[Organ Trafficking Ring Targeting Hikers]
<i>A despicable organ trafficking ring</i>

133
00:08:48,832 --> 00:08:50,026
[Busted by Police]
<i>that kidnapped hikers,</i>

134
00:08:50,026 --> 00:08:52,314
<i>harvested their organs,
and secretly buried their bodies</i>

135
00:08:52,314 --> 00:08:54,134
[Mount Taegong Missing Hikers]
<i>has been arrested by police.</i>

136
00:08:54,134 --> 00:08:55,518
[Confirmed Dead]
<i>It has been confirmed that</i>

137
00:08:55,518 --> 00:08:59,004
<i>all of the victims kidnapped
and murdered by the organization</i>

138
00:08:59,004 --> 00:09:00,578
<i>were hikers who had previously
been reported missing</i>

139
00:09:00,578 --> 00:09:04,411
<i>in the recent Mount Taegong
serial disappearance case.</i>

140
00:09:07,374 --> 00:09:09,945
<i>Police stated today that they have
recovered all of the victims' bodies,</i>

141
00:09:09,945 --> 00:09:14,878
<i>which were found buried in secluded
mountain areas across the country.</i>

142
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:17,345
[Illegal Organ Clinic Raided]
<i>Police conducted raids on hospitals</i>

143
00:09:17,345 --> 00:09:20,275
[All Involved Personnel Arrested]
<i>that purchased organs from them</i>

144
00:09:20,275 --> 00:09:24,978
<i>and performed illegal surgeries,
and arrested all involved parties.</i>

145
00:09:25,788 --> 00:09:29,526
<i>The police, having secured a list of
illegal organ transplant recipients,</i>

146
00:09:29,526 --> 00:09:32,870
<i>are expanding their investigation
across the entire medical sector.</i>

147
00:09:32,870 --> 00:09:35,388
<i>Authorities are also launching
a full-scale crackdown</i>

148
00:09:35,388 --> 00:09:37,146
<i>on illegal organ trafficking</i>

149
00:09:37,146 --> 00:09:40,250
<i>and pursuing other institutions
involved in similar crimes,</i>

150
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:43,745
<i>ensuring those responsible
face the full extent of the law.</i>

151
00:09:44,770 --> 00:09:47,445
<i>I hope they remember.</i>

152
00:09:47,445 --> 00:09:50,124
<i>Those who take their crimes lightly
and disregard the law</i>

153
00:09:50,124 --> 00:09:54,311
<i>should remember that
the harshest punishment comes for them</i>

154
00:09:54,311 --> 00:09:58,278
<i>when they feel the safest and most at ease.</i>

155
00:10:14,778 --> 00:10:19,934
Oh, I see. So you support Kingfisher? Got it.

156
00:10:19,934 --> 00:10:21,874
I understand your opinion.

157
00:10:21,874 --> 00:10:26,978
But as police officers, we have a duty
to stay true to our responsibilities.

158
00:10:29,646 --> 00:10:31,530
No, he said it was a tip-off call,
but instead of giving me anything,

159
00:10:31,530 --> 00:10:33,654
he just told me outright
not to catch Kingfisher.

160
00:10:33,654 --> 00:10:36,062
Oh, seriously...

161
00:10:36,062 --> 00:10:37,294
Hey, don't even mention it.

162
00:10:37,294 --> 00:10:39,378
Every time a major crime happens,

163
00:10:39,378 --> 00:10:41,722
people act like Kingfisher
is some kind of hero.

164
00:10:41,722 --> 00:10:45,374
Jeez, it's so distracting
that I can barely work.

165
00:10:45,374 --> 00:10:48,382
At most, it'll be another month or two.

166
00:10:48,382 --> 00:10:50,778
Something else will happen
somewhere soon, won't it?

167
00:10:52,402 --> 00:10:54,174
- Make sure the team leader eats well.
- Okay.

168
00:10:54,174 --> 00:10:55,947
We're heading out for a stakeout
in Inseong-dong.

169
00:10:55,947 --> 00:10:57,945
- Good luck.
- Yes, sir!

170
00:10:57,945 --> 00:10:59,410
[Violent Crimes Team 2]

171
00:10:59,410 --> 00:11:01,111
Take care.

172
00:11:04,386 --> 00:11:06,750
It's already this late...

173
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:08,934
Should we order dinner?

174
00:11:08,934 --> 00:11:10,890
The victims.

175
00:11:10,890 --> 00:11:12,870
Pardon?

176
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:16,711
When the perpetrator's side is blocked,
break through the victim's side.

177
00:11:17,950 --> 00:11:21,250
So far, Kingfisher's crime intervals
ranged from 7 to 60 days.

178
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:24,545
Like Mr. Jang said, another one
will happen somewhere soon.

179
00:11:24,545 --> 00:11:26,520
What if we chase the case

180
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:29,558
that's going to happen instead of
the one that's already happened?

181
00:11:29,558 --> 00:11:31,638
The case that's going to happen?

182
00:11:31,638 --> 00:11:33,630
Kingfisher's next target.

183
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:36,478
The next target? Who is it?

184
00:11:40,386 --> 00:11:41,762
No, I don't want to go.

185
00:11:41,762 --> 00:11:43,250
Why?

186
00:11:43,250 --> 00:11:46,245
You're going to a kids' cafe
with daycare today.

187
00:11:46,245 --> 00:11:47,586
It's going to be so much fun, isn't it?

188
00:11:47,586 --> 00:11:49,490
Mommy isn't coming.

189
00:11:49,490 --> 00:11:52,874
Yul, I told you I have to
go to work today, so I can't, right?

190
00:11:52,874 --> 00:11:53,938
That's right, Yul.

191
00:11:53,938 --> 00:11:56,230
Mommy has to go to work today,
so she can't go.

192
00:11:56,230 --> 00:12:00,334
Instead, I will buy you new
Baby Shark stickers tonight. Okay?

193
00:12:00,334 --> 00:12:02,545
No, don't buy me any.

194
00:12:04,406 --> 00:12:06,870
This won't do. Honey, you go ahead.

195
00:12:06,870 --> 00:12:08,858
You said you have to leave early
for a local assignment today. Hurry.

196
00:12:08,858 --> 00:12:10,258
It's still fine.

197
00:12:10,258 --> 00:12:12,638
We're going to get right up, right, Yul?

198
00:12:12,638 --> 00:12:14,434
No, I won't get up.

199
00:12:14,434 --> 00:12:15,470
Kwon Yul.

200
00:12:15,470 --> 00:12:18,226
If you don't get up
by the time I count to five,

201
00:12:18,226 --> 00:12:21,337
I'll pick you up myself and take you out.

202
00:12:21,337 --> 00:12:22,770
Do you want me to do that?

203
00:12:22,770 --> 00:12:24,314
No, don't!

204
00:12:24,314 --> 00:12:25,686
I'm counting.

205
00:12:25,686 --> 00:12:28,945
One, two...

206
00:12:28,945 --> 00:12:31,351
So scary. You should get up quickly, Yul.

207
00:12:31,351 --> 00:12:33,711
You know Mommy doesn't
go easy on you when she's mad, right?

208
00:12:36,678 --> 00:12:38,478
Three!

209
00:12:38,478 --> 00:12:40,794
Here it comes, four!

210
00:12:40,794 --> 00:12:44,245
Hmph, Mommy, no mercy!

211
00:12:50,206 --> 00:12:51,906
No mercy...

212
00:12:56,782 --> 00:13:00,054
My daughter is so smart.

213
00:13:00,054 --> 00:13:01,545
Give it to me.

214
00:13:01,545 --> 00:13:05,550
See? Mommy really doesn't go easy on you.

215
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:09,598
She's been that merciless since way back.

216
00:13:09,598 --> 00:13:14,278
When Daddy first met Mommy,
she was really scary.

217
00:13:15,385 --> 00:13:17,170
So scary. Let's go.

218
00:13:17,170 --> 00:13:19,311
So scary!

219
00:13:22,406 --> 00:13:26,878
Yul, what did Mommy tell you to do
at the kids' cafe today?

220
00:13:26,878 --> 00:13:27,878
Huh?

221
00:13:27,878 --> 00:13:31,645
Listen to your teacher.
Don't fight with your friends.

222
00:13:31,645 --> 00:13:34,678
And be careful not to get hurt, okay?

223
00:13:34,678 --> 00:13:37,254
That's what you need to do, got it? Okay?

224
00:13:37,254 --> 00:13:41,402
Oh? It's Seo Jun! Mommy, it's Seo Jun!

225
00:13:41,402 --> 00:13:43,829
- No.
- No, I...

226
00:13:43,829 --> 00:13:44,906
Huh?

227
00:13:44,906 --> 00:13:46,278
- I won't go.
- I'm late.

228
00:13:46,278 --> 00:13:48,978
I'm late. Let's go quickly.

229
00:13:49,986 --> 00:13:53,611
My car went in for repairs yesterday.

230
00:13:55,750 --> 00:13:58,606
I couldn't even get a taxi.

231
00:13:58,606 --> 00:14:01,206
My kid just picked today to throw a fit
about not wanting to go to daycare.

232
00:14:01,206 --> 00:14:03,286
You must have been at a loss.

233
00:14:03,286 --> 00:14:07,730
They say four is the difficult age.
That's exactly how my kid's been lately.

234
00:14:07,730 --> 00:14:09,906
Every morning is a battle.

235
00:14:09,906 --> 00:14:12,974
My commute is already a battle
since my office is so far away.

236
00:14:12,974 --> 00:14:15,082
My mommy goes to work too, right?

237
00:14:15,082 --> 00:14:16,974
That's right, Yul.

238
00:14:16,974 --> 00:14:19,118
Do you work too?

239
00:14:19,118 --> 00:14:23,378
I was on parental leave
and just recently returned to work.

240
00:14:23,378 --> 00:14:24,454
I'm just getting back into it.

241
00:14:24,454 --> 00:14:27,450
Oh, I didn't know.

242
00:14:27,450 --> 00:14:30,378
My mommy isn't coming to the kids' cafe.

243
00:14:30,999 --> 00:14:32,916
Right, Yul?

244
00:14:32,916 --> 00:14:36,611
It must be especially hard
since you've only just gone back.

245
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:38,886
After staying home with kids every day,

246
00:14:38,886 --> 00:14:42,811
going back to work must have you
feeling up and down lately, right?

247
00:14:43,778 --> 00:14:46,578
When you're just at home,
you miss the outside world.

248
00:14:46,578 --> 00:14:48,739
And when you're actually out working,
you worry about the child you left behind.

249
00:14:48,739 --> 00:14:50,111
Do you feel that way too?

250
00:14:50,111 --> 00:14:52,245
Oh, I was even worse.

251
00:14:52,245 --> 00:14:55,354
I had to leave my baby
when he was barely a year old.

252
00:14:55,354 --> 00:14:58,426
So days like today
make me feel especially guilty.

253
00:14:58,426 --> 00:15:01,078
The other moms all volunteer to go.

254
00:15:01,078 --> 00:15:02,650
I hate you, Mommy!

255
00:15:02,650 --> 00:15:03,962
Park Seo Jun.

256
00:15:03,962 --> 00:15:07,118
You shouldn't say such
mean things to your mommy.

257
00:15:07,118 --> 00:15:08,706
Funny, isn't it?

258
00:15:08,706 --> 00:15:10,376
I hate you, Mommy.

259
00:15:10,376 --> 00:15:12,570
Do you hate Mommy too, Yul?

260
00:15:12,570 --> 00:15:16,022
I'm sorry. What can I do?

261
00:15:16,022 --> 00:15:19,045
- I'd better get going.
- See you later, Ma'am.

262
00:15:21,606 --> 00:15:23,234
Why are they suddenly walking in together?

263
00:15:23,234 --> 00:15:26,690
Moms have to stick together
and look out for each other.

264
00:15:26,690 --> 00:15:27,770
How are you?

265
00:15:27,770 --> 00:15:29,942
Oh, hello.

266
00:15:29,942 --> 00:15:31,521
Hello, Miss.

267
00:15:31,521 --> 00:15:34,362
Oh, Seo Jun and Yul came together today?

268
00:15:34,362 --> 00:15:37,045
Hello, Miss.

269
00:15:38,918 --> 00:15:40,938
Hey, you!

270
00:15:40,938 --> 00:15:42,420
I'm sorry, Miss.

271
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:44,500
It's okay.

272
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:46,712
Please take good care of him today as well.

273
00:15:46,712 --> 00:15:50,238
Yul's mom, thank you so much today.

274
00:15:50,238 --> 00:15:51,278
I'll send you a coffee coupon.

275
00:15:51,278 --> 00:15:52,345
No, it's fine.

276
00:15:52,345 --> 00:15:54,811
- I'll get going first.
- Okay, take care.

277
00:15:54,811 --> 00:15:57,018
Yul, aren't you going to say bye to Mommy?

278
00:15:57,018 --> 00:15:58,372
Okay. My Yul.

279
00:15:58,372 --> 00:16:00,688
Today, too, with your friends,
get along well...

280
00:16:00,688 --> 00:16:02,878
Are you leaving without saying it?

281
00:16:02,878 --> 00:16:05,434
Don't worry too much, Ma'am.

282
00:16:05,434 --> 00:16:07,745
Please take good care of her, Miss.

283
00:16:11,570 --> 00:16:14,750
Oh, dear, Yul seems especially down today.

284
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:17,874
This is her way of protesting
against her mom.

285
00:16:17,874 --> 00:16:20,082
That must break her heart. What can she do?

286
00:16:20,082 --> 00:16:21,822
What do you mean by "what can she do"?

287
00:16:21,822 --> 00:16:24,911
Both mom and child have to get through it.

288
00:16:26,775 --> 00:16:27,801
[No talking while walking]

289
00:16:27,801 --> 00:16:30,645
Inmate 1503, Pyo Kyu Cheol, released!

290
00:16:35,578 --> 00:16:37,445
Do you have any belongings to collect?

291
00:16:40,314 --> 00:16:42,078
I don't need them.

292
00:16:49,646 --> 00:16:52,378
This punk is getting out now.

293
00:16:59,624 --> 00:17:03,680
[Durumi Electronics]

294
00:17:35,766 --> 00:17:37,070
Mr. Pyo Kyu Cheol.

295
00:17:37,070 --> 00:17:38,472
[Notice of Electronic Monitoring Order]
By court order, you'll be fitted

296
00:17:38,472 --> 00:17:41,247
with an electronic ankle monitor
starting now.

297
00:17:41,247 --> 00:17:43,259
Yeah...

298
00:17:43,259 --> 00:17:45,511
Just get this over with quickly.

299
00:17:53,271 --> 00:17:55,711
Darn, easy!

300
00:18:07,026 --> 00:18:08,914
Stop!

301
00:18:08,914 --> 00:18:11,045
Let's go!

302
00:18:13,298 --> 00:18:17,445
Easy. That's a big catch.

303
00:18:19,146 --> 00:18:21,678
That's it. Oh, my, how pretty.

304
00:18:21,678 --> 00:18:24,026
Yul, Yul!

305
00:18:24,026 --> 00:18:26,083
Yul, give me a V sign for the picture.

306
00:18:26,083 --> 00:18:28,445
You're not in the mood for a photo?

307
00:18:38,782 --> 00:18:39,782
Mommy!

308
00:18:39,782 --> 00:18:41,496
Shall Yul do this with Mommy?

309
00:18:41,496 --> 00:18:45,806
Here, look. Aim right at the mouse's head.

310
00:18:45,806 --> 00:18:48,271
Wow, Yul, look!

311
00:18:48,271 --> 00:18:50,167
Wow, it's going up.

312
00:18:50,167 --> 00:18:52,945
Wow, first place!

313
00:18:52,945 --> 00:18:55,478
Wow, Yul, good job!

314
00:18:57,810 --> 00:18:59,055
Careful.

315
00:18:59,055 --> 00:19:00,978
Look here! Here!

316
00:19:02,834 --> 00:19:06,346
Ye Geon, be careful! Come down carefully!

317
00:19:06,346 --> 00:19:08,346
They're still kids.

318
00:19:08,346 --> 00:19:11,642
You said you couldn't come.
How did you make it?

319
00:19:11,642 --> 00:19:13,394
Well, it wasn't anything urgent,

320
00:19:13,394 --> 00:19:15,746
so I asked my company
and took a half day off.

321
00:19:15,746 --> 00:19:16,878
Well done.

322
00:19:16,878 --> 00:19:21,511
How could you focus on work
after seeing her so upset?

323
00:19:22,318 --> 00:19:26,176
It'd be nice if kids understood
how their moms feel.

324
00:19:26,176 --> 00:19:28,745
Kids are all like that at this age.

325
00:19:28,745 --> 00:19:32,978
Their sense of self is developing,
but they're still self-centered at this age.

326
00:19:32,978 --> 00:19:36,970
They usually can't understand
others' perspectives until around age six.

327
00:19:36,970 --> 00:19:38,011
That's right.

328
00:19:38,011 --> 00:19:43,045
It's important to teach kids rules
and routines at this stage.

329
00:19:43,045 --> 00:19:45,822
But honestly, I find that so difficult.

330
00:19:45,822 --> 00:19:47,145
Me too, me too.

331
00:19:47,145 --> 00:19:51,011
Sometimes people tell you to be firm,
and other times they tell you to be gentle.

332
00:19:51,011 --> 00:19:54,218
They say you need to balance strictness
and kindness so kids don't get confused,

333
00:19:54,218 --> 00:19:56,516
but it's easier said than done, right?
Can you really do that?

334
00:19:56,516 --> 00:19:59,442
It's difficult. It's really hard.

335
00:19:59,442 --> 00:20:04,745
Still, they say this is
the most precious time for mom and kid.

336
00:20:04,745 --> 00:20:07,578
The memories that build the bond
between a kid and mom

337
00:20:07,578 --> 00:20:10,178
are created during this time.

338
00:20:13,282 --> 00:20:15,410
- Whoa!
- My baby, seriously...

339
00:20:16,566 --> 00:20:17,878
Ye Geon, careful!

340
00:20:17,878 --> 00:20:18,911
Be careful.

341
00:20:18,911 --> 00:20:22,076
What is this? Why is this punk getting out?

342
00:20:22,076 --> 00:20:23,524
What? Who's getting out?

343
00:20:23,524 --> 00:20:24,745
Pyo Kyu Cheol!

344
00:20:24,745 --> 00:20:26,242
- Look at this.
- <i>We are now at the prison entrance,</i>

345
00:20:26,242 --> 00:20:28,578
- <i>where tension has reached its peak.</i>
- Absolutely oppose Pyo Kyu Cheol's release!

346
00:20:28,578 --> 00:20:32,078
Since early dawn, many citizens
have been staging fierce protests.

347
00:20:32,078 --> 00:20:33,218
[Absolutely Oppose Pyo Kyu Cheol's Release]
Pyo Kyu Cheol, known as

348
00:20:33,218 --> 00:20:34,545
[Demand for Countermeasures]
one of the worst child sex offenders,

349
00:20:34,545 --> 00:20:37,122
is being released today
after serving 16 years.

350
00:20:37,122 --> 00:20:40,008
One of his victims was
an eight-year-old child,

351
00:20:40,008 --> 00:20:43,346
causing widespread shock and outrage.

352
00:20:43,346 --> 00:20:47,178
- Amend the Pyo Kyu Cheol Act!
- Although child sex crime laws

353
00:20:47,178 --> 00:20:48,545
were significantly strengthened in 2010,

354
00:20:48,545 --> 00:20:50,394
Pyo Kyu Cheol's crime occurred before 2009,

355
00:20:50,394 --> 00:20:53,026
when the previous law was still in effect,

356
00:20:53,026 --> 00:20:56,611
so he was released after serving
the relatively short sentence of 16 years.

357
00:20:56,611 --> 00:20:58,206
Outraged citizens

358
00:20:58,206 --> 00:21:01,038
called for the retroactive application
of the strengthened punishment law,

359
00:21:01,038 --> 00:21:02,858
- <i>leading to the so-called</i>
- Gosh! How could he do that

360
00:21:02,858 --> 00:21:04,418
- <i>Pyo Kyu Cheol Act amendment...</i>
- to an eight-year-old...

361
00:21:04,418 --> 00:21:06,546
The parenting forums
are already in an uproar.

362
00:21:06,546 --> 00:21:08,390
So this guy is getting out after all?

363
00:21:08,390 --> 00:21:09,938
- Why?
- Why do you think?

364
00:21:09,938 --> 00:21:12,108
He served his full sentence,
so they're letting him out.

365
00:21:12,108 --> 00:21:16,894
Then they should've given him
life in prison from the start.

366
00:21:16,894 --> 00:21:18,711
That's what I'm saying.
Isn't this totally insane?

367
00:21:18,711 --> 00:21:20,014
No, seriously...

368
00:21:20,014 --> 00:21:24,076
No, I mean, if it were up to me,
I'd call Kingfisher right this second.

369
00:21:24,076 --> 00:21:26,745
But I don't have his phone number.

370
00:21:26,745 --> 00:21:29,554
Oh, I'm so angry. What am I supposed to do?

371
00:21:29,554 --> 00:21:31,846
Seriously, how are we supposed
to live in a world like this?

372
00:21:31,846 --> 00:21:34,558
I'm so angry right now.

373
00:21:34,558 --> 00:21:36,854
- The law has to change. Seriously.
- What can we do?

374
00:21:36,854 --> 00:21:40,545
How can we let our kids go outside like this?

375
00:21:40,545 --> 00:21:42,278
I can't let them.

376
00:21:42,926 --> 00:21:44,722
As a dad raising a daughter,

377
00:21:44,722 --> 00:21:47,446
I felt I had to do something,
so I came out here.

378
00:21:47,446 --> 00:21:51,845
How can we let our kids go outside
when someone like that is released?

379
00:21:51,845 --> 00:21:54,478
Why should we be the ones living in fear?

380
00:21:54,478 --> 00:21:57,238
Yes, thank you for the interview.

381
00:21:57,238 --> 00:21:58,938
He's coming out!

382
00:21:59,745 --> 00:22:03,411
Pyo Kyu Cheol, you piece of trash!
Give him the death penalty!

383
00:22:19,559 --> 00:22:21,311
[Toward a Future-Ready Correctional System]

384
00:22:43,218 --> 00:22:45,411
That punk, seriously...

385
00:22:51,738 --> 00:22:53,878
- Let's go.
- Okay.

386
00:22:58,545 --> 00:23:02,211
I organized the previous victims
by crime type, as requested.

387
00:23:02,211 --> 00:23:04,858
As expected, murderers
make up the largest group.

388
00:23:04,858 --> 00:23:06,611
I figured.

389
00:23:07,402 --> 00:23:09,142
Oh, but that's strange.

390
00:23:09,142 --> 00:23:11,526
Why would Kingfisher leave
those kinds of people alone?

391
00:23:11,526 --> 00:23:13,738
Those kinds of people? What kind of people?

392
00:23:13,738 --> 00:23:17,918
People who prey on children.
People like child sex offenders.

393
00:23:17,918 --> 00:23:20,145
There wasn't a single one among his victims.

394
00:23:20,145 --> 00:23:23,511
Honestly, aren't those people the worst
when it comes to their crimes?

395
00:23:23,511 --> 00:23:25,198
Their rates of reoffending are high too.

396
00:23:25,198 --> 00:23:26,634
Beom.

397
00:23:26,634 --> 00:23:30,086
Track down child sex offenders
released in the past 15 years.

398
00:23:30,086 --> 00:23:32,278
Track them? What for?

399
00:23:32,278 --> 00:23:34,811
Whether they're still alive and well.

400
00:23:35,161 --> 00:23:36,248
[Violent Crimes Team 2]

401
00:23:42,114 --> 00:23:45,666
I narrowed down the worst child sex offenders
released over the past 15 years,

402
00:23:45,666 --> 00:23:47,578
and there are about eight of them.

403
00:23:47,578 --> 00:23:48,578
And?

404
00:23:48,578 --> 00:23:52,778
Here we go. Starting now,
here are three shocking facts.

405
00:23:54,062 --> 00:23:58,034
First, all eight of them are dead.

406
00:23:58,034 --> 00:24:00,442
- What?
- Second, how?

407
00:24:00,442 --> 00:24:01,830
They all died in accidents.

408
00:24:01,830 --> 00:24:06,006
Car crashes, drownings, falls,
electrocution, and so on.

409
00:24:06,006 --> 00:24:07,322
- Accidental deaths?
- Third.

410
00:24:07,322 --> 00:24:10,034
This is the most shocking part.

411
00:24:10,034 --> 00:24:15,211
They all died on the very day
they were released.

412
00:24:15,938 --> 00:24:18,578
This is pretty suspicious, right?

413
00:24:18,578 --> 00:24:20,945
This is like something from
"What on Earth," right?

414
00:24:21,698 --> 00:24:24,911
When is Pyo Kyu Cheol's release date?

415
00:24:25,738 --> 00:24:27,711
Pyo Kyu Cheol?

416
00:24:30,710 --> 00:24:34,207
Could Pyo Kyu Cheol really be
Kingfisher's next target?

417
00:24:34,207 --> 00:24:36,074
There's no evidence

418
00:24:36,074 --> 00:24:38,211
the dead child sex offenders
are connected to Kingfisher.

419
00:24:38,211 --> 00:24:40,445
I mean, it's not like
they were shot to death.

420
00:24:40,445 --> 00:24:42,162
It's too much of a coincidence to ignore.

421
00:24:42,162 --> 00:24:44,678
I'm just trying to grab onto any lead I can.

422
00:24:45,978 --> 00:24:50,182
We'll know if we keep an eye on him today.
Keep following him.

423
00:24:50,182 --> 00:24:51,882
Okay.

424
00:24:53,814 --> 00:24:58,431
Did you see that, Mr. Pyo Kyu Cheol?

425
00:24:58,431 --> 00:25:03,706
Those people are all parents with kids
protesting against your release.

426
00:25:03,706 --> 00:25:06,207
Nonsense.

427
00:25:06,207 --> 00:25:08,878
I mean, did I do anything to their kids?

428
00:25:09,578 --> 00:25:14,011
They should just watch their own darn kids.
What meddling is this?

429
00:25:15,845 --> 00:25:17,919
[Rest Area]

430
00:25:18,554 --> 00:25:22,146
We've got plenty of time.
Let's stop by a rest area.

431
00:25:22,146 --> 00:25:25,486
I've been out in the fresh air
for the first time in a while,

432
00:25:25,486 --> 00:25:28,322
and I need to take a dump.

433
00:25:28,322 --> 00:25:30,045
I'm saying I need to take a dump!

434
00:25:30,658 --> 00:25:33,958
Hey, I'm talking, dump!

435
00:25:33,958 --> 00:25:37,578
Right, you should make eye contact.

436
00:25:38,502 --> 00:25:40,202
Nice!

437
00:25:41,166 --> 00:25:43,886
Huh? It looks like they're
going into the rest area.

438
00:25:43,886 --> 00:25:46,078
- Go check.
- Yes.

439
00:25:56,646 --> 00:25:58,866
Are you even human?

440
00:25:58,866 --> 00:26:02,192
You're worse than an animal.

441
00:26:02,192 --> 00:26:05,978
Jeez, how could you do that
to innocent children?

442
00:26:07,598 --> 00:26:10,445
Oh, this punk really...

443
00:26:10,445 --> 00:26:13,345
If I weren't a reporter...

444
00:26:14,045 --> 00:26:16,306
I swear I'd slap you across the face!

445
00:26:16,306 --> 00:26:18,006
Mr. Kwon?

446
00:26:18,811 --> 00:26:20,845
What are you doing by yourself?

447
00:26:24,945 --> 00:26:27,111
I got a good shot.

448
00:26:27,111 --> 00:26:28,845
Want to see?

449
00:26:29,522 --> 00:26:31,970
I got all the protesters' interviews.

450
00:26:31,970 --> 00:26:33,559
Huh? Oh...

451
00:26:33,559 --> 00:26:34,902
Good work. How was it?

452
00:26:34,902 --> 00:26:39,038
They were all saying they can't raise
their kids in a world like this.

453
00:26:39,038 --> 00:26:40,645
They also said that at the very least,

454
00:26:40,645 --> 00:26:43,422
child sex offenders should receive
sentences of hundreds of years

455
00:26:43,422 --> 00:26:44,718
like in other countries.

456
00:26:44,718 --> 00:26:49,478
Sounds like they said exactly
what you're thinking, right?

457
00:26:53,550 --> 00:26:57,278
All parents feel the same way
when it comes to their children.

458
00:26:57,278 --> 00:26:58,278
Let's go.

459
00:26:58,278 --> 00:27:01,478
We need to check Pyo Kyu Cheol's
residence and the probation office.

460
00:27:02,206 --> 00:27:04,418
Yes.

461
00:27:05,486 --> 00:27:08,455
- Let's try blowing bubbles.
- Yul, look here! Look at Mommy.

462
00:27:08,455 --> 00:27:11,802
Seo Jun and Yul, look over here! Smile!

463
00:27:11,802 --> 00:27:15,011
Seo Jun, you look here too.

464
00:27:18,998 --> 00:27:20,978
You blew it well.

465
00:27:20,978 --> 00:27:22,510
Everyone, look this way.

466
00:27:22,510 --> 00:27:24,765
- Take a picture.
- Me too.

467
00:27:24,765 --> 00:27:26,312
- I want to blow too.
- What do you want to eat?

468
00:27:26,312 --> 00:27:27,362
Is it good?

469
00:27:29,110 --> 00:27:30,622
<i>Seo Jun's mom.</i>

470
00:27:30,622 --> 00:27:34,478
<i>Seo Jun is playing well, so don't worry.</i>

471
00:27:34,478 --> 00:27:35,938
<i>Oh, my, Yul's mom!</i>

472
00:27:35,938 --> 00:27:38,062
<i>Are you looking after our Seo Jun too?</i>

473
00:27:38,062 --> 00:27:40,645
<i>Oh, thank you so much.</i>

474
00:27:40,645 --> 00:27:42,110
<i>Did you go to the kids' cafe?</i>

475
00:27:42,110 --> 00:27:44,206
<i>You said you couldn't go.</i>

476
00:27:44,206 --> 00:27:46,982
<i>As expected, a mom knows a mom's heart best.</i>

477
00:27:46,982 --> 00:27:50,011
<i>Let's have a meal together
with the kids sometime.</i>

478
00:27:50,994 --> 00:27:53,111
Yul, play while eating this.

479
00:27:55,194 --> 00:27:56,230
Oh, no.

480
00:27:59,426 --> 00:28:00,486
What about this?

481
00:28:09,161 --> 00:28:12,859
[Samneung Rest Area, Men's Restroom,
Second Stall, Knock, Knock, Knock]

482
00:28:38,717 --> 00:28:40,886
This is getting ridiculous.

483
00:28:40,886 --> 00:28:45,440
Why do we have to politely drive a punk
like that all the way home?

484
00:28:45,440 --> 00:28:48,245
We're already severely short-staffed.

485
00:28:48,245 --> 00:28:49,949
I don't even know what I'm doing anymore.

486
00:28:49,949 --> 00:28:53,453
Are we monitoring this punk,
or protecting him?

487
00:28:53,453 --> 00:28:55,716
Oh, darn it.

488
00:28:55,716 --> 00:28:58,037
But is this guy making a darn masterpiece
in there or what?

489
00:28:58,037 --> 00:28:59,686
Why isn't he coming out?

490
00:29:03,169 --> 00:29:04,953
[Alert, Attempt to Remove Electronic Device]
What is this?

491
00:29:05,749 --> 00:29:06,749
Darn it!

492
00:29:10,025 --> 00:29:12,521
- Oh, what? What is it?
- Sorry.

493
00:29:18,693 --> 00:29:21,169
Mr. Lee, here!

494
00:29:21,169 --> 00:29:23,686
It says this punk is outside right now?

495
00:29:25,601 --> 00:29:28,336
Hey, did this punk escape through the window?

496
00:29:28,336 --> 00:29:30,053
Hurry! Let's go check!

497
00:29:38,173 --> 00:29:40,353
Huh? Sir, over there.

498
00:29:42,236 --> 00:29:43,289
This way.

499
00:29:43,289 --> 00:29:44,341
Okay.

500
00:29:44,341 --> 00:29:45,781
- Let's go.
- Yes.

501
00:29:45,781 --> 00:29:47,481
Wait!

502
00:29:54,377 --> 00:29:56,077
What about Pyo Kyu Cheol?

503
00:30:01,209 --> 00:30:03,437
He couldn't have gotten far.
Let's hurry and catch him.

504
00:30:03,437 --> 00:30:05,586
- Yes.
- Let's go!

505
00:30:08,041 --> 00:30:09,745
Ms. Gu, get in quickly.

506
00:30:09,745 --> 00:30:12,037
Huh? Mr. Kwon, what's going on?
Where are we going?

507
00:30:12,037 --> 00:30:14,853
I don't know, but something seems
to have happened to Pyo Kyu Cheol.

508
00:30:14,853 --> 00:30:16,553
Let's just go.

509
00:30:35,901 --> 00:30:38,186
Filthy punk...

510
00:30:44,997 --> 00:30:49,488
[Men's Restroom]

511
00:31:08,457 --> 00:31:12,886
Sir, welcome. Good work.

512
00:31:18,089 --> 00:31:22,405
Did Park Hee Dong send you by any chance?

513
00:31:22,405 --> 00:31:23,573
Of course.

514
00:31:23,573 --> 00:31:27,665
He's at Samjin Port right now.

515
00:31:27,665 --> 00:31:29,089
His name is Park Hee Dong.

516
00:31:29,089 --> 00:31:32,265
He was an inmate who was imprisoned
in the same cell as Pyo Kyu Cheol.

517
00:31:32,265 --> 00:31:33,527
Park Hee Dong served three years

518
00:31:33,527 --> 00:31:35,789
for producing and distributing
digital pornography

519
00:31:35,789 --> 00:31:37,505
and was released three months ago.

520
00:31:37,505 --> 00:31:39,129
Based on the information
we've gathered so far,

521
00:31:39,129 --> 00:31:41,953
after his release, Pyo Kyu Cheol
is expected to team up with Park Hee Dong

522
00:31:41,953 --> 00:31:44,320
to flee the country illegally,
establish a base there,

523
00:31:44,320 --> 00:31:46,861
and begin producing child pornography...

524
00:31:46,861 --> 00:31:49,782
Oh, jeez, crazy punk.

525
00:31:49,782 --> 00:31:51,740
Let's go straight into the scenario.

526
00:31:51,740 --> 00:31:54,224
We'll schedule the meeting
for the day of his release, as expected.

527
00:31:54,224 --> 00:31:56,497
But I think we should move up the timeline.

528
00:31:56,497 --> 00:31:58,181
Before he returns to his old neighborhood.

529
00:31:58,181 --> 00:32:01,083
During transport? That'll cause quite a stir.

530
00:32:01,083 --> 00:32:04,520
The child who was his last victim
still lives in that neighborhood.

531
00:32:07,261 --> 00:32:10,120
The Samneung rest area is 30 minutes
away from the prison here.

532
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:12,453
We'll intercept him during transport.

533
00:32:12,453 --> 00:32:14,453
And two hours away is Mount Jeonghan.

534
00:32:14,453 --> 00:32:17,020
There's a small birch forest here.

535
00:32:17,020 --> 00:32:20,253
It's a place Pyo Kyu Cheol would really hate.

536
00:32:21,249 --> 00:32:23,886
You have a pollen allergy.

537
00:32:24,775 --> 00:32:27,709
That's why I usually avoid mountains.

538
00:32:28,797 --> 00:32:31,153
[The patient has a history of allergies]
In spring, watch out for birch trees,

539
00:32:31,153 --> 00:32:33,853
and in autumn, you should
watch out for ragweed.

540
00:32:33,853 --> 00:32:36,820
I'll make the allergy medication.

541
00:32:36,820 --> 00:32:39,453
Give him a foretaste of hell.

542
00:32:39,453 --> 00:32:43,685
Alright, let's keep it simple.

543
00:32:43,685 --> 00:32:45,557
A guy just released from prison

544
00:32:45,557 --> 00:32:47,615
cuts off his electronic ankle monitor
and flees into the mountains.

545
00:32:47,615 --> 00:32:51,453
By chance, on a spring day,
while passing near a birch forest,

546
00:32:51,453 --> 00:32:55,083
he suffers an allergic attack
due to his chronic pollen allergy

547
00:32:55,083 --> 00:32:56,713
and falls to his death from a cliff.

548
00:32:56,713 --> 00:32:58,853
Oh, dear.

549
00:32:58,853 --> 00:33:02,785
Anyway, you've got yourself
some darn good friends.

550
00:33:02,785 --> 00:33:04,920
In life, it's not easy

551
00:33:04,920 --> 00:33:08,886
to meet someone
you click with so well, is it?

552
00:33:11,729 --> 00:33:15,320
Let me make one phone call.

553
00:33:16,525 --> 00:33:18,220
To where?

554
00:33:18,220 --> 00:33:20,786
Oh, your friend?

555
00:33:22,520 --> 00:33:24,986
You're so suspicious.

556
00:33:25,993 --> 00:33:27,693
Go ahead.

557
00:33:35,185 --> 00:33:35,645
[Mr. Park]

558
00:33:52,233 --> 00:33:54,553
<i>The subscriber you dialed...</i>

559
00:33:57,909 --> 00:33:58,865
[Calls Blocked, Confirmed]

560
00:34:00,021 --> 00:34:01,485
<i>The subscriber you dialed...</i>

561
00:34:01,485 --> 00:34:03,409
Oh, dear, seriously.

562
00:34:03,409 --> 00:34:04,889
You sure have a lot of free time.

563
00:34:04,889 --> 00:34:07,809
If you don't trust us,
you can just not get in!

564
00:34:07,809 --> 00:34:09,686
I won't go either then.

565
00:34:09,686 --> 00:34:11,786
Oh, my.

566
00:34:11,786 --> 00:34:15,853
No, I mean, Mr. Park offered good money

567
00:34:15,853 --> 00:34:19,279
and kept insisting that
he had to leave today.

568
00:34:19,279 --> 00:34:21,457
So I even canceled my own meeting
and came all the way here.

569
00:34:21,457 --> 00:34:24,566
And I even brought an expert
who can remove the ankle monitor.

570
00:34:24,566 --> 00:34:25,873
This ankle monitor?

571
00:34:25,873 --> 00:34:30,153
Oh, dear, not just anyone can remove it.
It's darn difficult!

572
00:34:31,253 --> 00:34:35,533
Fine, then stay here and wait around
until the police catch you.

573
00:34:35,533 --> 00:34:37,846
That's none of my business, okay?

574
00:34:37,846 --> 00:34:42,457
And you do know that if the client refuses,

575
00:34:42,457 --> 00:34:45,334
refunds are absolutely
impossible, right? Huh?

576
00:34:45,334 --> 00:34:47,917
You're way too suspicious.

577
00:34:47,917 --> 00:34:50,137
Hey, what are you doing?
Get in the car. I'm going home.

578
00:34:50,137 --> 00:34:51,953
We shouldn't have come here.

579
00:35:01,477 --> 00:35:05,679
Oh, dear, anyway, you picked a darn good day.

580
00:35:05,679 --> 00:35:09,909
This is exactly the kind of weather
that's perfect for leaving.

581
00:35:09,909 --> 00:35:13,353
Let's stop by the neighborhood
before we leave.

582
00:35:13,353 --> 00:35:18,901
What? Your house will be crawling
with people right now.

583
00:35:18,901 --> 00:35:22,924
If you go there,
you'll see things you shouldn't see.

584
00:35:22,924 --> 00:35:25,353
Who says I'm going home?

585
00:35:25,963 --> 00:35:29,526
Well, then where?

586
00:35:29,526 --> 00:35:34,820
Before leaving for a long journey,
I should at least see the kid's face once.

587
00:35:35,941 --> 00:35:39,981
I'm curious how much she's grown.

588
00:35:39,981 --> 00:35:45,353
She was about eight back then,
so after more than ten years...

589
00:35:46,702 --> 00:35:49,920
Wow, she must be all grown up
into a young lady.

590
00:35:58,309 --> 00:36:00,786
Do you really have to go that far?

591
00:36:15,353 --> 00:36:17,286
Manager Tae, nice!

592
00:36:21,014 --> 00:36:22,777
Oh, dear, he looks comfortable.

593
00:36:22,777 --> 00:36:24,853
Let's switch back again.

594
00:36:27,077 --> 00:36:30,020
Oh, dear, I guess I'm just
not suited for big cars.

595
00:36:46,583 --> 00:36:48,641
I've been wondering about something.

596
00:36:48,641 --> 00:36:51,501
Why do you use such complicated methods,
like staged accidents?

597
00:36:51,501 --> 00:36:53,985
It would be easier to just have
Kingfisher shoot them once.

598
00:36:53,985 --> 00:36:57,985
That would work, but there are
too many to handle alone.

599
00:36:57,985 --> 00:37:02,720
Especially since we're
in charge of the 'white' cases.

600
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:05,233
White...

601
00:37:05,233 --> 00:37:07,533
Why?

602
00:37:07,533 --> 00:37:10,353
A single shot, without pain,
clean and simple.

603
00:37:10,353 --> 00:37:11,953
That's Bo Na's way.

604
00:37:11,953 --> 00:37:13,957
I know that much.

605
00:37:13,957 --> 00:37:16,920
One shot, one kill.
Kingfisher's signature move.

606
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:19,053
Do you know why that is?

607
00:37:19,053 --> 00:37:20,753
Well, that's because...

608
00:37:21,813 --> 00:37:23,553
she's good at it?

609
00:37:25,481 --> 00:37:27,153
I think the driver must've gotten sleepy.

610
00:37:27,153 --> 00:37:28,108
[Drowsy Driving Rest Area]

611
00:37:28,417 --> 00:37:30,186
You should hurry.

612
00:37:39,697 --> 00:37:41,397
This is the truck.

613
00:37:43,657 --> 00:37:45,177
Beom, check the top.

614
00:37:45,177 --> 00:37:46,877
Yes.

615
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:55,087
Jeez. Oh, dear!

616
00:37:56,497 --> 00:37:57,886
This is the police!

617
00:37:57,886 --> 00:38:00,253
Stay where you are and please cooperate.

618
00:38:04,087 --> 00:38:05,161
Darn it!

619
00:38:13,285 --> 00:38:15,409
Oh, that scared me.

620
00:38:15,409 --> 00:38:17,686
I thought it was a dismembered body.

621
00:38:31,973 --> 00:38:36,486
After all this,
they just roughly dumped it and left?

622
00:38:41,565 --> 00:38:45,005
First, let's request assistance
from the highway patrol and local precincts

623
00:38:45,005 --> 00:38:46,669
and set up checkpoints
around the exits and entrances.

624
00:38:46,669 --> 00:38:49,020
We also need to secure
the rest area CCTV footage quickly.

625
00:38:49,020 --> 00:38:51,553
Let's move quickly. We don't have time.

626
00:38:55,001 --> 00:38:56,589
What?

627
00:38:56,589 --> 00:38:57,797
Kwon Tae Seong!

628
00:38:57,797 --> 00:38:58,853
What are you doing here...

629
00:38:58,853 --> 00:39:01,083
- Ms. Gu, hurry.
- Wait, wait!

630
00:39:01,083 --> 00:39:02,889
- Don't touch it.
- Hey, hey!

631
00:39:02,889 --> 00:39:04,420
Move the camera away, please.

632
00:39:04,420 --> 00:39:06,186
Hold on.

633
00:39:06,186 --> 00:39:07,920
Hey!

634
00:39:08,546 --> 00:39:10,862
Were you tailing me? Since when?

635
00:39:10,862 --> 00:39:12,665
Tailing? I just ran into you
at the rest area by chance.

636
00:39:12,665 --> 00:39:15,753
I'm on my way back
from covering Pyo Kyu Cheol's release.

637
00:39:15,753 --> 00:39:18,749
You lost Pyo Kyu Cheol, right? Huh?

638
00:39:18,749 --> 00:39:21,245
Is this related to Kingfisher?

639
00:39:21,245 --> 00:39:22,309
What?

640
00:39:22,309 --> 00:39:26,061
The Kingfisher detective is at the scene
where they lost Pyo Kyu Cheol.

641
00:39:26,061 --> 00:39:28,953
It's not even your jurisdiction.
You're a detective from Seoul.

642
00:39:29,788 --> 00:39:31,453
How do you have such good instincts?

643
00:39:31,453 --> 00:39:33,886
What's going on?

644
00:39:33,886 --> 00:39:35,620
Hey, this is...

645
00:39:36,453 --> 00:39:39,105
I'm only speculating at this point.

646
00:39:39,105 --> 00:39:40,897
I came here thinking
he might be the next target,

647
00:39:40,897 --> 00:39:42,073
but we got blindsided too.

648
00:39:42,073 --> 00:39:43,781
We need to find Pyo Kyu Cheol's
whereabouts first,

649
00:39:43,781 --> 00:39:45,686
whether he's dead or alive.

650
00:39:45,686 --> 00:39:48,063
Are you saying he might be dead?

651
00:39:48,063 --> 00:39:51,020
Don't jump to conclusions.
He could've just escaped.

652
00:39:51,020 --> 00:39:52,505
I'm busy, so just go on your way.

653
00:39:52,505 --> 00:39:54,285
You really can't do this.

654
00:39:54,285 --> 00:39:57,307
Mr. Kwon Tae Seong,
we're refusing your coverage from now on.

655
00:39:57,307 --> 00:39:59,120
Leave now.

656
00:39:59,120 --> 00:40:00,286
Don't take pictures!

657
00:40:00,286 --> 00:40:02,353
- Pack it up now.
- Okay.

658
00:40:05,553 --> 00:40:07,597
<i>The police have started moving.</i>

659
00:40:07,597 --> 00:40:10,153
They're conducting checkpoints
at the tollgate 20 kilometers ahead.

660
00:40:12,535 --> 00:40:14,257
You should get off the road now.

661
00:40:14,257 --> 00:40:16,541
Okay, let's take another route.

662
00:40:16,541 --> 00:40:18,286
Alright.

663
00:40:22,005 --> 00:40:23,075
Mommy will try it first.

664
00:40:27,381 --> 00:40:29,253
Yum, it's good!

665
00:40:32,961 --> 00:40:34,012
Is it tasty, sweetie?

666
00:40:34,012 --> 00:40:36,344
Yeah! It's super, super delicious!

667
00:40:36,344 --> 00:40:38,241
- Really?
- Yeah!

668
00:40:38,241 --> 00:40:40,855
You're in the best mood today, huh?

669
00:40:40,855 --> 00:40:41,913
Were you happy Mommy came?

670
00:40:41,913 --> 00:40:44,920
Yeah! I was so, so happy!

671
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:48,853
Then I should just quit going to work
and stay by your side every day, right?

672
00:40:48,853 --> 00:40:51,609
Well... No. You should work.

673
00:40:51,609 --> 00:40:54,473
Huh? I should work? Why?

674
00:40:54,473 --> 00:40:56,720
Because it's a necessary job.

675
00:40:57,797 --> 00:40:59,497
Huh?

676
00:41:02,059 --> 00:41:05,026
Daddy hasn't finished all his work yet.

677
00:41:05,026 --> 00:41:06,086
Should I sing you a song?

678
00:41:06,086 --> 00:41:08,009
What kind of work?

679
00:41:08,009 --> 00:41:12,237
Daddy is doing...
something very, very important.

680
00:41:12,237 --> 00:41:16,753
He is a truly good man
who does wonderful things for people.

681
00:41:16,753 --> 00:41:18,108
What about you?

682
00:41:18,108 --> 00:41:19,286
Huh?

683
00:41:19,286 --> 00:41:21,753
What do you do?

684
00:41:23,281 --> 00:41:25,520
I do...

685
00:41:30,705 --> 00:41:31,881
something necessary.

686
00:41:31,881 --> 00:41:33,581
Something necessary?

687
00:41:34,637 --> 00:41:36,353
Yeah.

688
00:41:37,909 --> 00:41:40,086
Something the world needs.

689
00:41:43,753 --> 00:41:46,253
Oh, my smart little girl.

690
00:42:19,904 --> 00:42:21,074
[Child on Board]

691
00:43:04,489 --> 00:43:06,386
We shouldn't have come here.

692
00:43:20,829 --> 00:43:21,953
<i>What's going on?</i>

693
00:43:21,953 --> 00:43:23,653
Team Leader!

694
00:43:47,720 --> 00:43:49,053
Move, hurry!

695
00:43:49,053 --> 00:43:50,786
Hurry!

696
00:43:58,473 --> 00:44:00,420
Team Leader, are you okay?

697
00:44:07,207 --> 00:44:08,986
Team Leader, are you okay?

698
00:44:08,986 --> 00:44:10,673
I'm fine.

699
00:44:10,673 --> 00:44:11,878
What about Pyo Kyu Cheol?

700
00:44:11,878 --> 00:44:14,020
We'll have to put things on hold
because of the witness issue.

701
00:44:14,020 --> 00:44:15,753
Catch Pyo Kyu Cheol quickly.

702
00:44:15,753 --> 00:44:17,306
- Catch him!
- Yes.

703
00:44:17,306 --> 00:44:21,053
Team Leader, you keep bleeding.
What should we do about your wound?

704
00:44:21,053 --> 00:44:23,086
- Oh, no.
- What should we do?

705
00:44:27,833 --> 00:44:29,720
Pull over! Stop the car!

706
00:44:34,260 --> 00:44:35,493
Do Woon, no!

707
00:44:35,493 --> 00:44:37,649
Do Woon! Do Woon!

708
00:44:37,649 --> 00:44:41,361
- I'm Pyo Kyu Cheol, you punks!
- Do Woon!

709
00:44:41,986 --> 00:44:44,986
Which mom, which dad
told them to kill me? Huh?

710
00:44:44,986 --> 00:44:49,120
I'm perfectly alive!
What is wrong with you all?

711
00:44:49,120 --> 00:44:51,353
You punks!

712
00:44:53,120 --> 00:44:54,837
Mommy...

713
00:44:54,837 --> 00:44:56,621
Who is this punk?

714
00:44:56,621 --> 00:44:59,573
Mommy...

715
00:44:59,573 --> 00:45:02,186
Do Woon!

716
00:45:03,957 --> 00:45:05,201
- <i>Team Leader.</i>
- Yeah.

717
00:45:05,201 --> 00:45:06,986
<i>Are you okay to drive?</i>

718
00:45:09,520 --> 00:45:11,257
Yeah, I'm still fine.

719
00:45:11,257 --> 00:45:13,220
Did you find Pyo Kyu Cheol?

720
00:45:14,025 --> 00:45:15,725
These punks...

721
00:45:18,057 --> 00:45:19,821
This punk hasn't been answering
his phone for a while.

722
00:45:19,821 --> 00:45:22,086
Answer the phone!

723
00:45:24,892 --> 00:45:26,886
What is this now?

724
00:45:29,486 --> 00:45:31,839
That punk...

725
00:45:31,839 --> 00:45:33,553
He couldn't have gotten far.

726
00:45:33,553 --> 00:45:35,817
Can you confirm the GPS location?

727
00:45:35,817 --> 00:45:37,517
Yes, I can.

728
00:45:40,201 --> 00:45:42,129
Looks like he's heading toward Incheon.

729
00:45:42,129 --> 00:45:44,562
He may be trying to catch a boat.

730
00:45:44,562 --> 00:45:45,562
What is this?

731
00:45:45,562 --> 00:45:48,386
What now? What is it?

732
00:45:49,240 --> 00:45:51,986
Jeez, that punk seriously...

733
00:45:53,069 --> 00:45:54,933
Mommy, I want gummies too. Gummies.

734
00:45:54,933 --> 00:45:58,487
Huh? Yul, but the doctor said that

735
00:45:58,487 --> 00:46:02,173
if you eat too many of those,
lots of bacteria will grow in your mouth.

736
00:46:02,173 --> 00:46:04,752
Then you'll have to go to the dentist again.
Are you okay with that?

737
00:46:04,752 --> 00:46:06,980
- No!
- You don't want that, right?

738
00:46:06,980 --> 00:46:10,581
Then how about we
grill some fish together today?

739
00:46:10,581 --> 00:46:12,221
How about mackerel, your favorite?

740
00:46:12,221 --> 00:46:13,453
I like mackerel!

741
00:46:13,453 --> 00:46:14,853
- Yul, this is mackerel...
- <i>This is a breaking news alert.</i>

742
00:46:14,853 --> 00:46:19,353
<i>Child sex offender Pyo Kyu Cheol,
released today after 16 years in prison,</i>

743
00:46:19,353 --> 00:46:23,701
<i>escaped during transfer after removing
his electronic ankle monitor.</i>

744
00:46:23,701 --> 00:46:27,959
<i>While police search for him
after issuing an emergency wanted notice,</i>

745
00:46:27,959 --> 00:46:28,981
[Vehicle Stolen, 3-Year-Old Boy]
<i>it has been confirmed that</i>

746
00:46:28,981 --> 00:46:30,333
[Taken Hostage Inside]
<i>Mr. Pyo stole a passing vehicle</i>

747
00:46:30,333 --> 00:46:32,101
- <i>and is fleeing with</i>
- Want mackerel?

748
00:46:32,101 --> 00:46:34,328
- <i>a three-year-old boy as a hostage.</i>
- Shall we go?

749
00:46:34,328 --> 00:46:38,149
<i>Police have found evidence that
Mr. Pyo attempted to make a call</i>

750
00:46:38,149 --> 00:46:40,869
- <i>using the vehicle owner's phone...</i>
- The police told us to come here.

751
00:46:40,869 --> 00:46:41,997
Is the child safe?

752
00:46:41,997 --> 00:46:44,486
Probation officers, please at least
let us know the current location.

753
00:46:44,486 --> 00:46:45,717
We can't find out either.

754
00:46:45,717 --> 00:46:47,420
This makes no sense!

755
00:46:47,420 --> 00:46:49,120
We're sorry.

756
00:46:53,259 --> 00:46:54,783
[Detective Lee Dong Jin]

757
00:46:55,561 --> 00:46:59,553
Sir, we haven't gotten much
on this side either.

758
00:47:00,586 --> 00:47:03,167
That punk, if he was going to run,
he should've gone alone.

759
00:47:03,167 --> 00:47:04,265
Why take a child?

760
00:47:04,265 --> 00:47:06,373
I'll find out what's happening
through my police contacts.

761
00:47:06,373 --> 00:47:09,349
Ms. Gu, go back
and look into the information.

762
00:47:09,349 --> 00:47:11,049
What?

763
00:47:13,745 --> 00:47:16,849
Mommy.

764
00:47:17,765 --> 00:47:21,027
Darn it! These persistent punks!

765
00:47:21,027 --> 00:47:22,930
You all know the priority, right?

766
00:47:22,930 --> 00:47:25,001
The child's safety comes first, so...

767
00:47:25,001 --> 00:47:28,497
<i>don't get too close or provoke him.</i>

768
00:47:28,497 --> 00:47:30,930
<i>Wait for the right opportunity
and take him down.</i>

769
00:47:30,930 --> 00:47:32,097
<i>Got it?</i>

770
00:47:32,097 --> 00:47:33,830
Yes.

771
00:47:34,730 --> 00:47:37,353
Keep quiet, you punk! Shut your mouth!

772
00:47:37,353 --> 00:47:41,691
Mommy.

773
00:47:58,629 --> 00:47:59,730
That punk, seriously.

774
00:47:59,984 --> 00:48:00,381
[Child on Board]

775
00:48:02,249 --> 00:48:04,197
Is he insane?

776
00:48:33,025 --> 00:48:34,013
[Bo Na]

777
00:48:39,819 --> 00:48:41,964
Mommy!

778
00:48:42,693 --> 00:48:43,985
Tae Min!

779
00:48:43,985 --> 00:48:46,230
Catch that punk!

780
00:48:51,497 --> 00:48:53,709
Hyun Nam, what about the child?

781
00:48:53,709 --> 00:48:55,233
Luckily, he doesn't seem injured.

782
00:48:55,233 --> 00:48:57,753
I'll take him to the car
and lay him down first.

783
00:48:57,753 --> 00:48:59,453
Let's go.

784
00:49:00,530 --> 00:49:02,364
Mommy...

785
00:49:41,087 --> 00:49:43,930
Ah, why? Come closer, come closer.

786
00:49:43,930 --> 00:49:45,563
Come closer, come closer!

787
00:49:45,563 --> 00:49:48,606
Why aren't you coming? Come here!

788
00:49:49,701 --> 00:49:52,861
You punks, you all thought I was a pushover.

789
00:49:52,861 --> 00:49:54,037
Try to kill me!

790
00:49:54,037 --> 00:49:55,797
Go ahead, try!

791
00:49:55,797 --> 00:49:59,757
I said kill me, you punks!

792
00:49:59,757 --> 00:50:02,564
I'm leaving!

793
00:50:28,629 --> 00:50:30,329
Meeting concluded.

794
00:50:45,597 --> 00:50:49,582
<i>Bo Na actually doesn't like seeing blood.</i>

795
00:50:49,582 --> 00:50:54,301
She also hates watching someone
die painfully right in front of her.

796
00:50:54,301 --> 00:50:56,630
That's why she prefers sniping.

797
00:50:56,630 --> 00:51:00,497
<i>She doesn't have to confront them up close,</i>

798
00:51:00,497 --> 00:51:02,296
<i>and it's not a method</i>

799
00:51:02,296 --> 00:51:06,673
<i>that involves unnecessary cruelty,
violence, or suffering.</i>

800
00:51:06,673 --> 00:51:11,589
It's only meant to make them
disappear from this world.

801
00:51:11,589 --> 00:51:13,564
The 'white' cases have been added too.

802
00:51:15,697 --> 00:51:19,464
<i>But people who hurt children were exceptions.</i>

803
00:51:19,464 --> 00:51:23,217
<i>That's why other team members
handled them until now.</i>

804
00:51:23,217 --> 00:51:24,596
<i>I don't know.</i>

805
00:51:24,596 --> 00:51:27,339
<i>Maybe she thought it was too easy a death,</i>

806
00:51:27,339 --> 00:51:31,664
<i>or maybe there was another reason.</i>

807
00:51:38,785 --> 00:51:40,630
<i>Anyway, today...</i>

808
00:51:41,797 --> 00:51:44,564
<i>in the end, Bo Na was the one who ended it.</i>

809
00:52:03,228 --> 00:52:04,409
[Not Today]

810
00:52:04,433 --> 00:52:06,881
They all died? How?

811
00:52:06,881 --> 00:52:11,173
[Summary of Subject Investigation]
Car accidents, falls, drownings.

812
00:52:11,173 --> 00:52:12,617
Another car accident?

813
00:52:12,617 --> 00:52:14,797
Wow, there's even electrocution.

814
00:52:14,797 --> 00:52:16,465
And what's strange is that

815
00:52:16,465 --> 00:52:20,064
[Release Date, Death Date]
they all died on the day they were released.

816
00:52:21,561 --> 00:52:23,864
Isn't that strange?

817
00:52:23,864 --> 00:52:26,930
If they'd been shot to death by Kingfisher,
I might understand.

818
00:52:26,930 --> 00:52:28,019
But how could every single one of them

819
00:52:28,019 --> 00:52:31,264
die unexpectedly on the day
they were released?

820
00:52:34,065 --> 00:52:36,530
- Call an ambulance. Now!
- Okay.

821
00:52:36,530 --> 00:52:40,458
You could say he died an unfortunate death.

822
00:52:40,458 --> 00:52:41,813
He was such a piece of work.

823
00:52:41,813 --> 00:52:45,964
Honestly, a guy like him getting gunned down
by the Kingfisher is just unsurprising.

824
00:52:46,339 --> 00:52:47,297
[Reporter Choi]

825
00:52:49,264 --> 00:52:51,864
Reporter Choi, what happened?
From the police...

826
00:52:51,864 --> 00:52:52,897
- <i>Breaking news.</i>
- What?

827
00:52:52,897 --> 00:52:54,230
- <i>After being released today,</i>
- Sir...

828
00:52:54,230 --> 00:52:55,230
- <i>he cut off his electronic</i>
- Sir!

829
00:52:55,230 --> 00:52:56,830
- <i>ankle monitor and fled...</i>
- Look over there.

830
00:52:56,830 --> 00:52:59,764
<i>He was found dead
after being shot by a sniper rifle.</i>

831
00:52:59,764 --> 00:53:01,997
<i>Mr. Pyo abandoned
the vehicle he stole and fled,</i>

832
00:53:01,997 --> 00:53:03,745
[Pyo Kyu Cheol,]
<i>but while attempting to escape</i>

833
00:53:03,745 --> 00:53:05,230
[Shot Dead by Sniper Rifle]
<i>on a fishing boat docked nearby,</i>

834
00:53:05,230 --> 00:53:10,264
<i>he was struck in the head by a bullet,
fell into the sea, and was found dead.</i>

835
00:53:11,041 --> 00:53:12,147
Even the blanket.

836
00:53:14,185 --> 00:53:16,221
Understood. Please make sure
the area is properly controlled.

837
00:53:16,221 --> 00:53:17,921
Thank you.

838
00:53:19,116 --> 00:53:20,730
Sir!

839
00:53:20,730 --> 00:53:22,873
The child was safely returned to his parents.

840
00:53:22,873 --> 00:53:25,327
They said he was lying on a sofa
in the management office,

841
00:53:25,327 --> 00:53:26,764
covered with a blanket.

842
00:53:26,764 --> 00:53:28,497
That's a relief.

843
00:53:31,085 --> 00:53:32,964
What's this really?

844
00:53:32,964 --> 00:53:35,597
It wasn't an accident,
and if it was a sniper shot, then this...

845
00:53:38,164 --> 00:53:40,230
I really don't know.

846
00:53:41,529 --> 00:53:45,964
Whether we were completely off track
or if we actually found the right answer.

847
00:53:49,561 --> 00:53:52,005
<i>I really feel sorry for Director Yoo.</i>

848
00:53:52,005 --> 00:53:54,789
We should've handled it somehow,

849
00:53:54,789 --> 00:53:58,781
but instead we made her
the target of the police again.

850
00:53:58,781 --> 00:54:02,717
A sniper shot can't really
be disguised as an accident.

851
00:54:02,717 --> 00:54:04,739
The bullet leaves evidence behind.

852
00:54:04,739 --> 00:54:07,264
Like Kingfisher's signature.

853
00:54:09,387 --> 00:54:12,321
Just hold on a little longer.
It's almost done.

854
00:54:12,321 --> 00:54:14,864
It's ironic, isn't it?

855
00:54:14,864 --> 00:54:16,993
That bullet puts Director Yoo in danger,

856
00:54:16,993 --> 00:54:19,864
but at the same time, it protects all of us.

857
00:54:19,864 --> 00:54:21,733
What do you mean by that...

858
00:54:21,733 --> 00:54:23,853
It's acting as a kind of decoy.

859
00:54:23,853 --> 00:54:25,991
It draws the investigation toward her.

860
00:54:25,991 --> 00:54:27,919
Because Director Yoo
is spectacularly drawing attention

861
00:54:27,919 --> 00:54:29,421
under the name Kingfisher.

862
00:54:29,421 --> 00:54:32,261
So other cases can quietly
disappear from the spotlight.

863
00:54:32,261 --> 00:54:34,821
The Musan case last time was like that too.

864
00:54:34,821 --> 00:54:38,164
So that puts Director Yoo
in the most dangerous position.

865
00:54:38,164 --> 00:54:40,664
She's also the most likely to get caught.

866
00:54:40,664 --> 00:54:41,664
Bingo.

867
00:54:41,664 --> 00:54:45,693
That's why we're all sorry
and grateful to Director Yoo.

868
00:54:45,693 --> 00:54:50,697
But no one else could do what she does.

869
00:54:50,697 --> 00:54:53,230
She's the most capable among us.

870
00:54:54,102 --> 00:54:55,802
It's done.

871
00:54:56,525 --> 00:54:58,225
Good work.

872
00:55:03,628 --> 00:55:04,693
Here you go.

873
00:55:05,997 --> 00:55:08,725
Oh, you didn't have to pay this much.

874
00:55:08,725 --> 00:55:12,363
And you really don't have to be
this generous every time.

875
00:55:12,363 --> 00:55:15,997
You rushed over from the library
while writing your thesis.

876
00:55:15,997 --> 00:55:17,125
I feel especially bad today.

877
00:55:17,125 --> 00:55:20,469
Actually, I was just dozing off.

878
00:55:20,469 --> 00:55:22,553
Did the matter you went to handle
get resolved well?

879
00:55:22,553 --> 00:55:24,993
The client suddenly filed a complaint, right?

880
00:55:24,993 --> 00:55:28,785
Thanks to you, it was resolved well.
Thank you.

881
00:55:28,785 --> 00:55:30,565
Mommy!

882
00:55:30,565 --> 00:55:32,264
Did our Yul wake up?

883
00:55:32,264 --> 00:55:33,869
Yul!

884
00:55:33,869 --> 00:55:37,845
She seemed a little down,
and then she suddenly fell asleep.

885
00:55:37,845 --> 00:55:40,361
Really? You did?

886
00:55:40,361 --> 00:55:43,630
I'm sorry I left when I promised
I'd spend today with you.

887
00:55:44,837 --> 00:55:47,430
You can just give me lots of hugs.

888
00:55:48,269 --> 00:55:50,369
Of course, I will hug you like this.

889
00:55:50,369 --> 00:55:52,664
Come on, hug me too.

890
00:55:55,018 --> 00:55:57,464
How is it, Yul? Do you feel better?

891
00:55:57,464 --> 00:56:00,930
Yeah, I feel better. What about you?

892
00:56:01,805 --> 00:56:03,505
Me?

893
00:56:04,945 --> 00:56:06,764
I'm okay too.

894
00:56:08,130 --> 00:56:11,797
When I'm holding Yul like this, I'm okay.

895
00:56:25,369 --> 00:56:28,069
Wow, this time it's a sniper?

896
00:56:28,069 --> 00:56:29,797
Again on the day of release?

897
00:56:29,797 --> 00:56:32,564
Sir, what is this?

898
00:56:33,577 --> 00:56:37,261
This seems to be related to Kingfisher.

899
00:56:37,261 --> 00:56:39,364
<i>Shouldn't we dig into it?</i>

900
00:57:07,360 --> 00:57:10,045
The sender's address is from Russia.

901
00:57:10,045 --> 00:57:12,741
Yeah, it was sent by a friend.

902
00:57:12,741 --> 00:57:14,664
Yul! Look at this!

903
00:57:14,664 --> 00:57:17,618
Your mommy's friend
sent you a doll as a gift.

904
00:57:17,618 --> 00:57:20,362
- Yul is lucky.
- Wow, it's mine!

905
00:57:20,362 --> 00:57:21,530
Mommy, give it to me.

906
00:57:21,530 --> 00:57:23,626
Here.

907
00:57:23,626 --> 00:57:26,085
It's mine!

908
00:57:26,085 --> 00:57:27,785
Cute.

909
00:57:31,377 --> 00:57:34,029
Oh, these are Russian letters.

910
00:57:34,029 --> 00:57:36,357
What does it say, Bo Na?

911
00:57:36,357 --> 00:57:37,497
Just a greeting.

912
00:57:37,497 --> 00:57:41,065
Things like "How have you been?"
and "I miss you."

913
00:57:41,065 --> 00:57:42,679
Oh, I'm jealous.

914
00:57:42,679 --> 00:57:45,725
You have a friend who even
sends you gifts from overseas.

915
00:57:45,725 --> 00:57:48,197
Indeed, having good friends is nice.

916
00:58:52,175 --> 00:58:53,944
[Caller ID Restricted:
You keep your promises well]

917
00:58:53,944 --> 00:58:55,333
[Good. Another good night, Tae Seong]

918
00:59:44,530 --> 00:59:47,393
[A Bona Fide Killer]

919
00:59:47,417 --> 00:59:50,560
When did we get a new member
of the family without me knowing?

920
00:59:50,560 --> 00:59:52,164
They sent a gift from Russia.

921
00:59:52,164 --> 00:59:54,598
They say they'll be coming to Korea soon.

922
00:59:54,598 --> 00:59:57,417
He's the notorious youngest son
of the so-called Royal Family.

923
00:59:57,417 --> 00:59:58,730
Why were you acting up?

924
00:59:58,730 --> 01:00:00,009
We need to look into it now.

925
01:00:00,009 --> 01:00:03,997
Whether it was just an accident
or an unjust death disguised as one.

926
01:00:03,997 --> 01:00:06,197
Anyway, Chairman Cheon Seong Gyu
is at the center of it.

927
01:00:06,197 --> 01:00:10,089
This feels like a terrifying case
with a complicated web of connections.

928
01:00:10,089 --> 01:00:13,661
Sniping isn't the only method
Kingfisher uses.

929
01:00:13,661 --> 01:00:14,897
A joint investigation?

930
01:00:14,897 --> 01:00:16,127
I'll handle this.

931
01:00:16,127 --> 01:00:17,973
It's too dangerous for you
to be exposed at the scene, Bo Na.

932
01:00:17,997 --> 01:00:18,789
[Mother]

933
01:00:18,789 --> 01:00:20,605
- Mother.
- It's our family's memorial rite,

934
01:00:20,605 --> 01:00:22,169
yet you're making
the daughter-in-law do all the work?

935
01:00:22,169 --> 01:00:23,413
I think this is unfair.

936
01:00:23,413 --> 01:00:25,113
You little punk...

937
01:00:26,501 --> 01:00:29,230
Yul! Yul is missing!
